    "result_text": "The full test suite passes: **282 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner registration limit in the owner creation endpoint.\n\n**Change** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- In `addOwner`, after the duplicate checks and before persisting, added a call to a new helper `isDailyRegistrationLimitReached()`. When it returns true, the endpoint responds with `400 Bad Request`.\n- The helper counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals today (`LocalDate.now()`) and returns true once that count reaches 20 \u2014 so the 21st registration for the day is rejected.\n\n**Tests** (`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.java`):\n- `createOwnerRejectedWhenDailyLimitReached` \u2014 seeds 20 owners registered today, then verifies a further POST returns 400.\n- `createOwnerAllowedWhenBelowDailyLimit` \u2014 seeds 19 owners registered today and verifies one more is still created (201), confirming the boundary.\n\nThe limit is keyed on registration date, and seeded owners have a null `registration_date`, so they don't count toward the daily cap.",
